cff-version: 1.2.0
title: PERSEUS Forest Intelligence
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aaron
    family-names: Weiskittel
    email: aaron.weiskittel@maine.edu
    affiliation: "Center for Research on Sustainable Forests, University of Maine"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2534-4478"
abstract: >-
  CONUS multi-model forest carbon, value and risk decision-support tool covering
  all 48 conterminous states with deep focal coverage for Maine, Indiana, and
  Georgia (plus multi-engine series for Minnesota, Oregon, Washington, and
  Idaho), forest health, risk and resilience, harvest and stumpage economics,
  permanence risk, wood products carbon, FIA remeasurement AGB yield curves and
  relative density thresholds. Built on the perseus_db carbon-pool-harmonized
  database. Static React + Vite application deployed via GitHub Pages.
repository-code: "https://github.com/holoros/perseus-forest-intelligence"
url: "https://holoros.github.io/perseus-forest-intelligence/"
